I added the rule to `.mahou/write-documentation.md`. When a change's prototype shows a screen that already has one in `app/docs/prototipos/`, the existing prototype gains the new functionality instead of a new file being added.

For this change, that means:
- **`inicio-responsive.html`** gains the questions panel on the featured card, "Otras sesiones", the timeline check marks, and the case with no featured session.
- **`admin-sesion.html`** gains:
  - the "Destacada" switch;
  - the enable modal;
  - the confirmations;
  - the "Preguntas destacadas" switch;
  - Activar appearing only on the featured session.
- **`admin-sesiones.html`** gains the "Destacada" label in the session list.

`card-preguntas.html` and `profe-destacada.html` stay in the scratch folder as the source for those updates.

For the new announcement item, I'm going with your confirmation: it points to the session, its name is the session title, and its email line reads `Se abrieron las preguntas de la sesión "<título>".`

One decision is still open before I run `write-documentation`. Should `invariantes.md` gain the rule that every student write on a session requires it to be the featured one, or should the change only update the other seven notes?

I'll add the invariant along with the other seven note updates.

An Opus agent is drafting all the documentation changes in `.scratch/preguntas-en-la-card/docs-draft/`. It covers:
- the 8 notes, including the new rule in `invariantes.md`: "Toda escritura del estudiante sobre una sesión exige que sea la sesión destacada";
- updated copies of `inicio-responsive.html`, `admin-sesion.html` and `admin-sesiones.html`;
- the index rows that change.

Nothing is written to `app/docs` yet. When the draft is back, I'll review it, run the wording and conventions checks, and show you the whole thing before anything lands.

I told `docs-draft` to do the visual check itself once its prototype subagents finish, without launching any more subagents. For each of the three updated prototypes it will:
- open the file in the browser and confirm the console shows no errors;
- screenshot each new state and modal and compare them with the same state in `card-preguntas.html` or `profe-destacada.html`;
- confirm the states that already existed still look the same as in the original in `app/docs/prototipos/`;
- fix anything that overlaps, gets cut off or doesn't match the brief, and check it again.

Its final report will have one line per file saying what it checked and what it fixed.

