I attached the sessions to trail #3. Your decisions are being applied in the "decisions kurasu" tab (Sonnet high).

**Why Entire recorded nothing:** every subagent inherits `ENTIRE_PI_NESTED=1` from my process. The probe subagent showed it set even with the `.pi` extension present. The project's Entire extension for pi reads that mark as "nested pi" and stops sending events, so the subagents' commits got no checkpoint. It wasn't a problem with enabling Entire in the worktree: the git hooks are shared through the main `.git`.

**What I did:** I attached each transcript to the last commit of its stage on `feat/preguntas-en-la-card`. The transcripts stay under `~/.pi/agent/sessions/` even after the worktree is deleted.

| Session | Commit |
|---|---|
| Implementer | `docs(web): say featured…` |
| Validation | the B24 fix |
| Review, plus its 42 reviewers (tagged as review) | the review's last commit |
| Consistency check and reconciliation fixes | `refactor(database)…` |

Each attach rewrote that commit and every later one; the content didn't change and nothing was pushed. The subagent now running and this session are still missing. I'll attach them on the last commit when it finishes.

**`.mahou/implement.md`:** I replaced the "Supervisor session" step with "Sessions on the trail", which records:
- why Entire records nothing during an implement run;
- where the transcripts are, how to attach each session, and that the supervisor goes last;
- that commits are looked up by subject, because attaching rewrites them;
- that the step is your go-ahead to use `--force` on unpushed commits of the change's branch.

